{"name":"Green Envy","hex":"#77aa00","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"green","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of grass and leaves; a primary additive color midway between yellow and blue which is evoked by light between roughly 495–570 nm.","A member of a green party; an environmentalist."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a green hue.","Sickly, unwell."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/green"},{"term":"envy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Resentful desire of something possessed by another or others (but not limited to material possessions). .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","An object of envious notice or feeling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To feel displeasure or hatred towards (someone) for their good fortune or possessions.","To resentfully or discontentedly desire (something someone else has that one lacks)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/envy"}],"entries":[{"title":"Envy","blocks":[{"text":"Envy is an emotion which occurs when a person lacks another's quality, skill, achievement, or possession and either desires it or wishes that the other lacked it. Envy can also refer to the wish for another person to lack something one already possesses so as to remove the equality of possession between both parties."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg/330px-The_mad_woman-Theodore_Gericault-MBA_Lyon_B825-IMG_0477.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Envy","wikidata":"Q188739"},{"title":"Green","blocks":[{"text":"Green is the color between cyan and yellow on the visible spectrum. It has 295–350 different shades. It is evoked by light which has a dominant wavelength of roughly 495–570 nm. In subtractive color systems, used in painting and color printing, it is created by a combination of yellow and cyan; in the RGB color model, used on television and computer screens, it is one of the additive primary colors, along with red and blue, which are mixed in different combinations to create all other colors. By far the largest contributor to green in nature is chlorophyll, the chemical by which plants photosynthesize and convert sunlight into chemical energy. Many creatures have adapted to their green environments by taking on a green hue themselves as camouflage. Several minerals have a green color, including the emerald, which is colored green by its chromium content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg/330px-Champ_de_bl%C3%A9_C%C3%B4te-d%27Or_Bourgogne_avril_2014.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Green","wikidata":"Q3133"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg/330px-Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9b/Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg/330px-Giotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Invidia, allegorical painting by Giotto di Bondone, c. 1305–1306","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGiotto_-_Scrovegni_-_-48-_-_Envy.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/22/Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg/500px-Jheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_%28Invidia%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Hieronymus Bosch, The Seven Deadly Sins and the Four Last Things (Invidia)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJheronimus_Bosch_Table_of_the_Mortal_Sins_(Invidia).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg/500px-Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg/1280px-Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg/500px-Vauxhall_Vagabond_%281953%29_%2833320873386%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Advertisement using envy to promote sales","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVauxhall_Vagabond_(1953)_(33320873386).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Spanish_jewellery-Gold_and_emerald_pendant_at_VAM-01.jpg/500px-Spanish_jewellery-Gold_and_emerald_pendant_at_VAM-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Spanish_jewellery-Gold_and_emerald_pendant_at_VAM-01.jpg/500px-Spanish_jewellery-Gold_and_emerald_pendant_at_VAM-01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpanish_jewellery-Gold_and_emerald_pendant_at_VAM-01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Rotbugara_2010.JPG/500px-Rotbugara_2010.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Rotbugara_2010.JPG/1